      "name": "Tau Pathology and Neurofibrillary Tangles",
      "description": "Hyperphosphorylation of tau protein leads to the formation of intracellular neurofibrillary tangles, which are toxic to neurons and correlate with disease severity and progression in Alzheimer\u2019s disease. Elevated CSF total tau (TAU) and phosphorylated tau (PTAU) reflect ongoing neurodegeneration and are prominent in MCI and AD diagnoses. This mechanism is fundamental in disrupting microtubule stability, contributing to neuronal death and cognitive impairment.",
