      "name": "Neurodegeneration and Brain Atrophy",
      "description": "AD is characterized by progressive loss of neuronal tissue, with significant atrophy of hippocampus, entorhinal cortex, fusiform, and middle temporal areas, as well as ventricular enlargement. MRI-derived measures (e.g., hippocampal and entorhinal volume, whole brain volume, ventricular volume) serve as robust biomarkers for disease staging and diagnosis, reflecting both severity and regional patterns of neurodegeneration associated with memory and executive dysfunction.",
